I've heard this before, but I think there's probably a bunch of people who don't know that bronosaurus never actually existed. Like, it's still kind of in the top five of dinosaurs that people know. But actually, it was an apatosaurus the whole time, which is the wrong skull. Yeah, so the actual name Brontosaurus went unused by paleontologists for around 100 years. And it actually wasn't even until 1979 that the Carnegie Museum corrected the head on its own skeleton. But I am sure that there are some listeners out there who are dinosaur enthusiasts. And when Bronosaurus came up in the main story, thought, that's not even a real dinosaur. Right.
